From: BeeWi BC7PW bring-up <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] mt7601sta: trace wext_notify_event_assoc()

Third instrumentation level, temporary. Level two bracketed the fault to the
call of wext_notify_event_assoc() from StaAddMacTableEntry() (marker A8
printed, A9 did not, caller's guard intact in r7/r8). These markers bracket
the two steps inside it, so the log says whether execution dies in the copy
or in the event send:
  WXTRAP entry        on entry, with the IE length
  WXTRAP 1-after-copy after NdisMoveMemory into the local buffer
  WXTRAP 2-after-send after RtmpOSWrielessEventSend returns

--- a/common/rt_os_util.c
+++ b/common/rt_os_util.c
@@ -135,13 +135,16 @@
 	IN UINT32 ReqVarIELen)
 {
 	char custom[IW_CUSTOM_MAX] = {0};
+	printk(KERN_ERR "WXTRAP entry len=%u\n", (unsigned)ReqVarIELen);
 
 #if WIRELESS_EXT > 17
 	if (ReqVarIELen <= IW_CUSTOM_MAX)
 	{
 		NdisMoveMemory(custom, ReqVarIEs, ReqVarIELen);
+		printk(KERN_ERR "WXTRAP 1-after-copy len=%u\n", (unsigned)ReqVarIELen);
 		RtmpOSWrielessEventSend(pNetDev, RT_WLAN_EVENT_ASSOC_REQ_IE, -1, NULL,
 								(UCHAR *)custom, ReqVarIELen);
+		printk(KERN_ERR "WXTRAP 2-after-send\n");
 	}
 	else
 	    DBGPRINT(RT_DEBUG_TRACE, ("pAd->StaCfg.ReqVarIELen > MAX_CUSTOM_LEN\n"));
